really different than the experience of serious mental illness. So how to deal with the stigma of suicide in that life. And then we're working with a colleague on fetal alcohol spectrum disorder to remind people, if you don't know if you're pregnant, you should not drink alcohol. Actually, oversimplify it. Alcohol is a grotesque poison compared to almost anything else. And so that leads to significant developmental disorders, actually to a degree greater than the presence of autism. And the problem is it makes natural sense. What's wrong with you? How could you drink?
